  "body": "## Problem\n\nOn `origin/main` (merge `31f8d03d7` and later), two test targets of `camcraft-app` do not compile:\n\n```\nerror[E0063]: missing field `basis_version` in initializer of `operation::types::params::Tilt`\n   --> crates\\app\\src\\posting_section_mode.rs:133:35\nerror[E0063]: missing field `basis_version` in initializer of `camcraft_app::operation::Tilt`\n   (test \"section_mode\")\n```\n\n- `crates/app/src/posting_section_mode.rs` (lib unit test, line 133).\n- `crates/app/tests/section_mode.rs`.\n\n## Cause\n\nCommit `5b23f102b` (G93 inverse-time feed and section mode markers) writes `Tilt { a_deg, b_deg, origin }` literals. Commit `a7b438241` (PR #2157) adds the field `basis_version` to `Tilt`. Each side merged clean, but the result does not build.\n\n## Effect\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib` fail on main. The lib release build is not affected.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `basis_version` (the current value, or `..Default::default()` if `Tilt` has a default) to the two literals.\n\nFound during the refresh of PR #2187.\n",
